    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "1c5653d9caa0d44ca7580d5a56d4e5e24717cf2cacecd6b4db3066a147b1a9a4",
      "text": "Day 5 · After breakfast, a visit to the Brazilian side of the falls along the canyon of the Iguaçu River, in a national park of unique flora and fauna. The name of the falls means “big water” in Guarani: some 275 cascades, each with its own name, plunge with a roar into the gorge of the Devil’s Throat, amid spray and rainbows. On the way to the most powerful of them, you pass many smaller falls and magnificent landscapes. Optional: the Bird Park or the Macuco Safari.",
